# JavaFX (HabiTV)

Applies to GUI modules (`trayView`, `habiTv`). Runtime is still **Java 8 +
JavaFX 2.x** (`jfxrt`) unless an explicit migration task says otherwise.

- Keep UI code in tray/GUI packages; business/download logic stays in
  `application/core` and plugins.
- Do not block the JavaFX Application Thread with network or heavy I/O.
  Background work: patterns like `FxBackgroundRunner`; UI updates via
  `Platform.runLater`.
- Controllers live under `…/controller/`; follow existing listener and
  lifecycle patterns in the same package.
- Prefer existing resource/FXML loading helpers; do not invent a second
  UI framework or migrate OpenJFX in a non-migration PR.
- Remove listeners/subscriptions when controllers tear down if the file
  already does so for similar hooks.
